cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use dom-api-tracer, please cite it using the metadata below. When
  the journal article on warpdom is published, please cite the article
  (preferred-citation).
type: software
title: "dom-api-tracer: measure which DOM APIs real test suites use"
version: 0.1.0
# DOI: assigned by Zenodo at the v0.1.0 release; add it here afterwards.
# doi: "10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX"
# date-released: "YYYY-MM-DD"  (the v0.1.0 release date)
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/sonukapoor/dom-api-tracer"
url: "https://github.com/sonukapoor/dom-api-tracer"
authors:
  - family-names: Kapoor
    given-names: Sonu
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-6074-6238"
abstract: >-
  dom-api-tracer plugs into Vitest or Jest, instruments the DOM
  implementation the tests run on (jsdom or happy-dom), and records
  every DOM method call, property read and property write per test file,
  which a CLI aggregates into a usage report across files and projects. It
  also contains the research harness used to evaluate warpdom: a pinned
  corpus of open-source projects, scripts that run each project's own test
  suite traced and untraced under different DOM environments, and the
  timing, correctness and profiling workflows.
keywords:
  - DOM
  - jsdom
  - happy-dom
  - testing
  - Vitest
  - Jest
  - instrumentation
  - API usage
  - benchmarking
references:
  - type: software
    title: "warpdom: a fast, jsdom-compatible DOM for unit and component tests"
    authors:
      - family-names: Kapoor
        given-names: Sonu
    repository-code: "https://github.com/sonukapoor/warpdom"
    # doi: "10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX"
    notes: >-
      The DOM implementation that dom-api-tracer's measurements informed and
      evaluated.
